From 93cdf3c35681062f1137e699cf745139b115c4be Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oscar <osm1019@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 16:27:16 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] dodge: Add Gallery/Photos open-target chooser to OplusCamera

Stock hardcodes com.oneplus.gallery as the target for the thumbnail tap and for
"view last shot", so on a build where the user prefers Google Photos the camera
still bounces them into OppoGallery2, and on a build shipping no OppoGallery2 at
all the intent simply fails.

Adds ho/gallery_target, a small helper that resolves the preferred handler and
falls back to the stock package when nothing better is installed, then routes the
two call sites through it:
- k6/dg.smali a() returned the hardcoded package name; it now asks
  gallery_target.preferredOrDefault().
- GalleryHelper started the intent with Activity.startActivity() directly; it now
  goes through gallery_target.launch(), which retargets the intent and still
  honours the ActivityOptions bundle.

Keeping the resolution in one helper means the fallback behaviour is identical for
both entry points, rather than duplicating the package check at each call site.
